      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following curves is simple, closed, and positively oriented?",
      "worked_solution": "A simple closed curve is positively oriented if, when traveling along it, one always has the curve interior to the left and the curve exterior to the right. Otherwise, the curve is negatively oriented. \n\nA curve is positively oriented if it is traversed counterclockwise and is negatively oriented if it is traversed clockwise. \n\nAmong the given options, the only positively oriented simple closed curve is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14190405/assets/03fca239767a3b71681507bd861161147c1b39e90ee827b57dc74dcd66eaf24c.png)",
